Design a circuit that decodes a 4-bit binary input into a 7-segment display code. The module takes a 4-bit input representing a decimal digit (0 to 15) and outputs the corresponding 7-bit representation to drive a 7-segment display, where each output bit controls an individual segment of the display. The case statement maps each possible input value to a specific output pattern, allowing for the visualization of hexadecimal digits and their corresponding display encoding, defaulting to displaying '0' when an invalid input is provided.
