Design a 4-bit up/down counter that increments or decrements its value based on a control input. When the U_D input is high, the counter counts up; when U_D is low, it counts down. The counter state is updated on the rising edge of the clock, using pipelined registers to store the intermediate states. The output is a 4-bit value representing the current count.
