Design a digital logic circuit that outputs Y based on a combination of inputs from A1, A2, B1, B2, and C1. The circuit utilizes two AND gates to produce intermediate signals from the inputs B1 and B2, and A1 and A2, respectively. These outputs are then fed into a NOR gate along with input C1, which results in the final output Y after passing through a buffer. The overall functionality represents a logical operation that combines the results of the AND gates and the NOR gate to determine the output based on the specified input conditions.
module top_module(
    // module ports
    output Y,
    input A1,
    input A2,
    input B1,
    input B2,
    input C1
);

