Design a 16-bit barrel shifter that allows for parallel data shifting in both left and right directions based on a 4-bit shift amount. The module takes a 16-bit input data and a 4-bit input representing the number of shift positions. It performs a series of right shifts on the data through multiple stages and outputs the appropriately shifted 16-bit result. The final output concatenates the relevant bits from the last stage to achieve the desired shift capability, effectively implementing a versatile bitwise operation for data manipulation in digital circuits.
